    "result_text": "The full build passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the level rules with a points system across three files:\n\n**`MembershipLevel.java`** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/`) \u2014 reworked to compute points, then map points to a level:\n- `pointsForOwner(Owner)`: starts at 0, `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` household of 3+, `+3` tenure over 365 days (using the existing `householdSize` field on `Owner`).\n- `levelForPoints(int)` / `forOwner(Owner)`: maps points to level \u2014 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+). Keeping `forOwner` intact preserves the existing audit-log call in `OwnerRestControllerV1`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `membershipPoints` (via `pointsForOwner`) alongside the existing `membershipLevel` mapping, so both fields are returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema property (`minimum: 0`) and updated `membershipLevel` (new `maximum: 4` and description) so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `membershipPoints` field.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` \u2014 an owner with email + unique name, single-member household, zero tenure \u2014 asserts `membershipPoints=3` (2+1) and `membershipLevel=2`. The full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures.",
